# unit-marker-column.rq — the accounting currency-marker column (AXIOM, open world).
# A grid column ?col is a UNIT MARKER for its right neighbor iff:
#   (1) it has >=1 tab:CurrencyGlyph cell, and every non-Blank cell in it is a
#       CurrencyGlyph carrying the SAME symbol text (Blank cells are wildcards
#       here, but this OWN-COLUMN purity check deliberately does NOT extend the
#       wildcard to tab:ParenthesizedNumber the way the split/homogeneity queries'
#       datatypeAbstains normalisation does: this asks "is anything ELSE present
#       in the column?", not "what type is the column?", and a parenthesized
#       number is a present, real value that genuinely disqualifies a marker
#       column — R63, ruled 2026-08-06, not an oversight);
#   (2) SAME-ROW form (final-review fix, I1): there exists at least one row ?r such
#       that column ?col carries a CurrencyGlyph AT THAT ROW, and the right neighbor
#       column (?col + 1) carries a non-blank Numeric or Currency cell ON THE SAME
#       ROW ?r — the "$ beside its value" shape. Any-row (the pre-fix form) would let
#       a numeric YEAR HEADER over an all-text body license absorption; the marker
#       must sit beside a value it actually marks. The neighbor check compares the
#       NORMALISED datatype family (tab:inDatatypeFamily) — ?tn = tab:Quantity —
#       rather than enumerating tab:Numeric/tab:Currency, so it tracks the loop's
#       own family rule instead of drifting from it; abstaining datatypes never
#       satisfy it.
# Presence-based: no distance, no count, no tolerance. The symbol set lives in the
# emitter's is_currency_glyph (B2b's shipped [$€£¥] class, reused — no new constant);
# this query reads only the emitted tab:CurrencyGlyph datatype facts.
# Consumed by unitmarker.derive_marker_columns; evidence = unitmarker.marker_evidence.
PREFIX tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#>
SELECT DISTINCT ?col ?sym WHERE {
  ?c1 tab:atGridColumn ?col ; tab:atGridRow ?r ; tab:cellDatatype tab:CurrencyGlyph ; tab:gridText ?sym .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?cx tab:atGridColumn ?col ; tab:cellDatatype ?dx .
    FILTER(?dx != tab:CurrencyGlyph && ?dx != tab:Blank)
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?cy tab:atGridColumn ?col ; tab:cellDatatype tab:CurrencyGlyph ; tab:gridText ?sy .
    FILTER(STR(?sy) != STR(?sym))
  }
  BIND(?col + 1 AS ?nc)
  FILTER EXISTS {
    ?cn tab:atGridColumn ?nc ; tab:atGridRow ?r ; tab:cellDatatype ?dnraw .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?dnraw tab:datatypeAbstains true }
    OPTIONAL { ?dnraw tab:inDatatypeFamily ?dnfam }
    BIND(COALESCE(?dnfam, ?dnraw) AS ?tn)
    FILTER(?tn = tab:Quantity)
  }
}
ORDER BY ?col
